  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>The University of Redlands, established in 1907, is a private university located in Redlands, California. It offers diverse undergraduate and graduate programs and is accredited by the Western Association of Schools and Colleges (WASC). The university has a beautiful campus that spans 160 acres.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>At the University of Redlands, you’ll be part of a supportive student community. The Student Involvement and Success (SIS) office offers various extracurricular activities to enrich your university experience. You can engage in over 80 student-led clubs and organisations, including community service initiatives, outdoor programs, and 21 NCAA Division III athletic teams.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>At the University of Redlands, you'll find a variety of housing options designed to suit your preferences. If you prefer off-campus living, the university offers off-campus apartments as well. &nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:center;\"><i>Additionally, if you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, feel free to </i><a href=\"https://edvoy.com/app/\"><i>download our app</i></a><i> and check out the Stays feature!</i></p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p><strong>Library</strong><br>The Armacost Library offers extensive online and physical resources, including books, e-books, journals, and more. The library also features study areas and quiet zones for individual study and spaces for group work.</p><p><strong>Sports</strong><br>You can use several athletic facilities at the university. These include the Thompson Aquatic Centre for swimming and aquatic activities, Currier Gymnasium, Ted Runner Stadium, a fitness centre, and much more. You can also be part of the university’s athletic sports, by participating in the university’s NCAA Division III athletic sports teams.</p><p><strong>Cafeteria</strong><br>The University of Redlands Dining provides you with various options on campus. The university also provides flexible meal plans to cater to different lifestyles and dietary preferences. The Table at Irvine Commons is your main spot for campus dining.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
